# 094 · Copy an ID from any page

**Status:** `DROPPED`, merged into [243](_completed/243-web-app-base.goal) · **Version:** [v0.3.0](../roadmap.md#v030)

## What

Next to each ID the dashboard shows (a campaign, a run, a rig, a lane, a trial, an attempt, an experiment, a command, a rule, a message), a small **Copy** button copies it with one click, with a short "Copied" in place. A second choice copies a reference that names where it is, such as `rig-1 / run-1 / attempt a-…`, or the page's link, so it can be pasted into a chat with an agent ("look at this part of the system") or sent to someone.

## Why

The owner, 2026-10-22: "There should be a "copy id" of things like run, campaign, worker, lane etc. So that you can copy it to reference in chats or sending links etc... I don't have a good way to copy something quickly and pass it in and say "take a look at this part of the system to figure out xyz"."

## Done when

- [ ] A mockup, approved by the owner, of where the buttons sit and what each copies.
- [ ] The buttons on every page that shows those IDs, with keyboard use and a test that each copies the right text.
- [ ] The pages that describe the dashboard.

## Decisions

- 2026-10-22, owner: in v0.1.1.
- 2026-10-24, owner: v0.1.1 becomes the code clean-up; this goal moves to v0.1.4, the UI clean-up and UX improvements.
- 2026-11-09, the owner: v0.2.0 ships what was built ("cut v0.2.0 with what changes we have now"); this goal, not started, moves to v0.3.0 with the new features.
- 2026-11-10, the owner, with the v0.3.0 plan (goal [242](_completed/242-v030-review.goal)): merged into [243](_completed/243-web-app-base.goal). Every ID can be copied in the new dashboard, from its base (goal 243).

## Open questions

- Whether the reference copied is plain text, a link, or both on one click.

## Progress

- 2026-10-22: Goal written from the owner's request.
- 2026-11-10: Merged into goal 243.

